WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.851
Phase 4 brings each cloud under the
plane, and its real contribution is the

2
00:00:04.851 --> 00:00:09.888
validation matrix: every class of name
resolves correctly from every origin.

3
00:00:09.888 --> 00:00:13.323
A private endpoint name
returning a public address from

4
00:00:13.323 --> 00:00:17.124
anywhere is a failed test, even
if the application seems to work.

5
00:00:17.124 --> 00:00:21.361
Phase 5 is the one step whose
mistakes can't be cheaply undone,

6
00:00:21.361 --> 00:00:23.225
so it's gated, not scheduled.

7
00:00:23.225 --> 00:00:28.501
All five gates must pass, including locator
records resolving at one hundred percent

8
00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.284
for thirty consecutive days,

9
00:00:30.284 --> 00:00:34.000
and ninety days of parallel
running with no critical alerts.

10
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.829
Then decommission in order,
archiving the final exports

11
00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:41.250
before anything is removed,
with a seven-day burn-in.

12
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:46.990
Losing locator records early causes
forest-wide sign-in and domain-join failures.
